  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {口|くち}ごたえをする (talk back)\n- {口|くち}ごたえするな (don't talk back)\n- {親|おや}に{口|くち}ごたえする (talk back to one's parents)\n\nUSAGE:\nAlways carries a negative connotation — it implies insubordination or rudeness from someone who should show deference. The command {口|くち}ごたえするな is a classic phrase heard from parents and authority figures. Can be written as {口答|くちごた}え with kanji, though the hiragana form ごたえ is more common. Not to be confused with {歯|は}ごたえ (bite, texture of food) or {手|て}ごたえ (response, feedback).",
